P-3 (spec 017, the night shift; plan.md §2 and §10; tasks.md T066): the night shift's three roles, defined where
every role is.

What governs what: the .claude/agents/ files, their tools lines, and the hook's scopes govern a DAYTIME subagent of
that type in your own sessions. The night's sessions are main sessions (no agent_type) and run under their settings
layers, deploy/night-shift/claude/<role>.settings.json, and their prompts, deploy/night-shift/runner/prompts/<role>.md.
The layers are broader than these tools lines (each allows Bash; the gate-runner's allows Edit on /night/io/out/
only); the container is the night's boundary. Each agent file says so in its last sentence.

What it changes:
  - .claude/agents/supervisor.md, studio.md, gate-runner.md (new), in the existing files' frontmatter and length, each
    mirroring its night prompt and plan.md §2's role table:
      supervisor   Read, Grep, Glob, Write, Edit, and git add/commit/status/log/diff: read-mostly; it writes only
                   queue.json and docs/night-shift/<date>.md, and starts nothing;
      gate-runner  Read, Grep, Glob, Write: read-only on the repository; it writes only its io folder's outbox,
                   /night/io/out/, and asks the runner for main's gate, never --prove;
      studio       Read, Grep, Glob, Edit, Write, Bash: its edit tools write only /night/io/out/ and
                   /srv/studio/handoff/; it renders in /srv/studio/outputs/ through Blender and ComfyUI; it uses only
                   the tools the brief lists, and starts ComfyUI only through the runner.
  - .claude/agents/ops.md: one sentence on asking the runner for a plan (the request's shape, the plan-only role, and
    "off" until you turn plans on).
  - tools/gates/roles.expected: the three tools lines, which evals/agent-config/static.py compares.
  - .claude/hooks/protected-paths.sh, scope(): each new role's write scope, as enforced: supervisor, queue.json and
    docs/night-shift/ (relative to its worktree); gate-runner, /night/io/out/ only; studio, /night/io/out/ and
    /srv/studio/handoff/ only; the last two by the absolute path, both resolutions. scope() now takes the absolute path
    as its second argument. Its hunks are far from P-1's in the same file: both apply in either order (checked).
  - redteam/forbidden-actions.sh: the roster check names the nine roles; seventeen role rows for the three (each sent
    with and without an agent_id, as every role row is), allow and block on each side of each scope, with `..` and a
    sibling folder; the both-forms count goes from 7 types to 10. Its hunks are far from P-5's: both apply in either
    order (checked).
  - tools/gates/matrix-required.txt: ten of the new role rows.
Without the roster and roles.expected lines, the agent files alone would fail the matrix and the static evals, so they
travel together here.

Spec IDs: plan.md §2 (the roles), FR-015, his Q10 answer (amend the constitution: P-9, whose clauses say what this
patch enforces), Q13.

Needed for: plan and gate on, with P-2 and P-6.

How to apply, on your own branch, from the repository's root (one line each):
  B=feat/017-g5-patches
  F=docs/merge-requests/2026-11-12-feat-017-p3.patch
  git show "refs/heads/$B:$F" > /tmp/p3.patch
  sha256sum /tmp/p3.patch
  patch -p1 --dry-run < /tmp/p3.patch
  patch -p1 < /tmp/p3.patch
The patch touches .claude/, so the gate's agent-config-evals step waits for make evals-agent-config.

Verified on a fresh `git archive refs/heads/main` export (main d4870ec8): dry run and apply clean; main's
evals/agent-config/static.py: "0 failed, 0 planned", all nine roles matching roles.expected; bash -n and shellcheck -x
clean on the hook and the matrix; `bash redteam/forbidden-actions.sh`: 1024 passed (the unpatched export: 990),
25 failed, 65 known gaps, "every listed row ran". The 25 are stage S's, the same 25 the unpatched export fails (an
export isn't the sandboxed checkout). With all eleven patches: see the index.

